            </article>
        </section>

        <section class="section-heading fade-up">
            <h2>Frequently Used Guide Sections</h2>
            <p>Browse the most important legal and travel information for pets.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="guide-content">
            <article id="adoptionSection" class="guide-box fade-up">
                <div class="guide-box-title">Pet Adoption Laws in Jordan</div>
                <div class="guide-box-body">
                    <h3>Adoption Rules for Companion Animals</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Responsible Adoption:</strong> Adoption should be done as a humane and committed act.</li>
                        <li><strong>Owner Responsibility:</strong> The adopter must provide proper healthcare, safety, nutrition, and a stable environment.</li>
                        <li><strong>Contract Importance:</strong> Adoption agreements may include terms related to care, follow-up, and long-term responsibility.</li>
                        <li><strong>Animal Welfare:</strong> The owner is expected to follow animal welfare standards and avoid neglect.</li>
                        <li><strong>Lifelong Commitment:</strong> Adopting a pet means providing care and protection throughout its life.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article id="travelSection" class="guide-box fade-up">
                <div class="guide-box-title">Pet Travel Regulations</div>
                <div class="guide-box-body">
                    <h3>Traveling With Pets To and From Jordan</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Basic Documents:</strong> A microchip, valid rabies vaccine, and pet passport or travel documents may be required.</li>
                        <li><strong>Vaccinations:</strong> Rabies vaccination should usually be completed before travel within the required time frame.</li>
                        <li><strong>Health Certificate:</strong> Some destinations require an official health certificate issued by an approved veterinarian.</li>
                        <li><strong>Additional Tests:</strong> Some countries may ask for antibody or blood tests before entry.</li>
                        <li><strong>Airport Procedures:</strong> Confirm airline rules, crate size, and approval timelines before travel day.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="mini-grid">
                        <div class="mini-card">
                            <h4>Travel Checklists</h4>
                            <p>Passport, microchip, vaccine record, crate, permit documents.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mini-card">
                            <h4>Health Requirements</h4>
                            <p>Vaccination schedule, health check, fit-to-travel approval.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mini-card">
                            <h4>Airline Guidelines</h4>
                            <p>Cabin rules, cargo rules, carrier dimensions, destination notes.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article id="lawsSection" class="guide-box fade-up">
                <div class="guide-box-title">Comprehensive Guide to Pet Laws and Procedures</div>
                <div class="guide-box-body">
                    <h3>Main Legal and Travel Procedures</h3>

                    <div class="table-wrap">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Procedure</th>
                                    <th>Details & Documents</th>
                                    <th>Fees & Time</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Entering Jordan</td>
                                    <td>ISO microchip, rabies certificate, health certificate.</td>
                                    <td>Approx. 5 JOD / around 1 hour</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Export Permit</td>
                                    <td>Pet passport, owner ID, service department review.</td>
                                    <td>Approx. 5 JOD / around 1 hour</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Import Permit</td>
                                    <td>Pre-import approval and certificate of origin if needed.</td>
                                    <td>Approx. 10 JOD / 1–3 days</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Transit Permit</td>
                                    <td>Transit application through airport or border authority.</td>
                                    <td>Approx. 10 JOD / 1–3 days</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Traveling by Air</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>In-Cabin Pets:</strong> Allowed depending on airline rules, pet size, and carrier dimensions.</li>
                        <li><strong>Checked Baggage:</strong> Subject to airline conditions and limited availability.</li>
                        <li><strong>Restricted Breeds:</strong> Some breeds or animals may have transport restrictions.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Traveling to the United States</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Dogs Only:</strong> Some countries require additional entry review for dogs.</li>
                        <li><strong>CDC Form:</strong> A dog import form may be required depending on origin and timing.</li>
                        <li><strong>Timing:</strong> Apply early to avoid delays before departure.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Adoption & Responsibility</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Adoption fees may vary depending on organization and care history.</li>
                        <li>Vaccinations, sterilization, and microchipping may already be included.</li>
                        <li>Responsible ownership remains the main legal and ethical requirement.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </article>
        </section>

